<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Wip on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/wip/</link><description>Recent content in Wip on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 13 Feb 2015 18:10:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/wip/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Gidolinya</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/123278/</link><pubDate>Fri, 13 Feb 2015 18:10:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/123278/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I started making alternates for Gidole and as someone also pointed out in that thread it looked more like a separate font.&lt;br&gt;
So I made it into it&amp;rsquo;s own font (borrowing some characters from Gidole) and would love some feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More screenshots over at: &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317112050/https:/www.behance.net/gallery/23391815/Gidolinya-Free-Typeface" title="https://www.behance.net/gallery/23391815/Gidolinya-Free-Typeface"&gt;https://www.behance.net/gallery/23391815/Gidolinya-Free-Typeface&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317112050im_/http:/typophile.com/files/Gidolinya2_4046.png" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Gidole sans</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/121996/</link><pubDate>Sun, 14 Dec 2014 10:16:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/121996/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110824im_/http:/typophile.com/files/Lettering_5376.png" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m creating this and would love some feedback. The typeface will be free and with multiple weights when done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I haven&amp;rsquo;t done any kerning and the spacing is very rough. Focus right now is on getting the glyphs as I want them and trying to do some optical corrections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See the pdf&amp;rsquo;s for more detail and sample text.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317110824im_/http:/typophile.com/files/behance_6343.png" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
